WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.887
The workbook chapter lists six
dangers, and each has a guard.

2
00:00:03.887 --> 00:00:08.426
A GCC High or DoD tenant read on
the worldwide host returns nothing,

3
00:00:08.426 --> 00:00:13.790
and the gate passes on an empty list; the
guard is the cloud named in the settings,

4
00:00:13.790 --> 00:00:17.751
the session guard, and every
request on the cloud's own host.

5
00:00:17.751 --> 00:00:22.659
A next link to another host would send the
token somewhere the agency didn't choose;

6
00:00:22.659 --> 00:00:25.475
next links are followed
only on the cloud's host.

7
00:00:25.475 --> 00:00:29.828
A broad Graph scope for convenience
would let the reader change the tenant;

8
00:00:29.828 --> 00:00:32.637
it holds two read permissions,
declared per call.

9
00:00:32.637 --> 00:00:36.533
A kit rule mistaken for Microsoft's
deadline would give a post

10
00:00:36.533 --> 00:00:40.276
with no date an invented one;
the action basis names the rule.

11
00:00:40.276 --> 00:00:43.295
Data privacy posts go unseen
by the reader's role,

12
00:00:43.295 --> 00:00:45.937
so name a privacy reader
where they matter.

13
00:00:45.937 --> 00:00:48.084
And look-alike email gets acted on,

14
00:00:48.084 --> 00:00:51.994
so the task links the post the kit
read from Graph, as the intake,

15
00:00:51.994 --> 00:00:57.580
triage and routing chapter of Compliance
Automation and Day-Two Operations requires.
